{
  "artifacts": [
    {
      "path": "data/clean/cleaned_data.csv",
      "type": "CSV",
      "description": "Cleaned and aligned daily time series of precipitation (mm) and stream discharge (cfs) from 2015-01-01 to 2020-12-31."
    }
  ],
  "user_friendly_explanation": "The script loaded two raw datasets—one for daily stream discharge and one for daily precipitation—parsing their dates and setting up a continuous daily calendar from January 1, 2015 through December 31, 2020. It then merged these series on the common date index. Missing values within the series were filled by linear interpolation over time: any remaining precipitation gaps were set to zero (reflecting dry days), and any lingering gaps in discharge were filled by carrying the last known value forward or backward. Finally, the cleaned and aligned data (with columns date, precipitation_mm, and discharge_cfs) were written out to data/clean/cleaned_data.csv. A minor FutureWarning noted the deprecation of the current fillna method calls, but it didn’t affect the successful creation of the cleaned dataset."
}

