Log‐Transformed Model Performance  
To address the heteroscedasticity observed in the residuals of the raw‐space model, a second LSTM was trained to predict the natural logarithm of discharge (with a +0.1 offset). After exponentiation of both true and predicted values, evaluation on the same 2020 test set yielded an improved NSE of 0.72 and an RMSE of 3,100 cfs, as recorded in outputs/log\_metrics.json. The back‐transformed predictions more accurately track both low‐flow and high‐flow dynamics, demonstrating enhanced capacity to capture flashiness.

